From b8e5de10b0b800efeb71afb583f828bfdadc6eab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:37:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] Round 2: Reuse persistent pool threads for parallel
 batches

Replace per-batch scoped worker threads with helper threads that live
for the process and wait on a condition variable between batches. The
calling thread works on its own batch alongside up to workers - 1
helpers through the same atomic index and per-index result slots, so
records stay in input order. Concurrent batches share the pool and may
grow it up to 63 helpers; panics propagate to the caller; a forked
child process gets a fresh pool.

Workload: parallel (96 full records, four workers, 2-vCPU host), 11
samples against round 1.
Before median: 0.648 ms. After median: 0.493 ms. Speedup: 1.31x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
